.\n\n## 2. Data model\n\nAll persisted state is read and written through one store module (backend/src/store.js) backed by loadJson/saveJson in a single db file. Collections and fields:\n\n- users: id, username (unique, 1-39 lowercase ASCII), email (unique), passwordHash, verified, createdAt.\n- sessions: token, userId, createdAt.\n- organizations: id, name (unique lowercase), displayName (trimmed 1-100), createdAt.\n- orgMemberships: id, organizationId, userId, role ('owner' or 'member').\n- teams: id, organizationId, name, parentTeamId (nullable, must be a team in the same organization).\n- teamMemberships: id, teamId, userId.\n- repositories: id, organizationId, name, visibility ('public' or 'private'), createdAt.\n- repoGrants: id, repositoryId, granteeType ('user' or 'team'), granteeId, role ('read', 'triage', 'write', 'maintain', 'admin').\n\nRelationships: an organization Owner is an orgMembership with role 'owner'. Team membership is independent of organization membership, but only accounts that are organization members can be added to teams. A team grant on a repository applies only to direct members of that team; parent/child team hierarchy never carries membership. Removing an organization member atomically deletes their org membership, all their team memberships in that organization, and all their direct repo grants in that organization; team grants themselves remain.\n\n## 3. Seed plan\n\nSeed only when the data file does not exist. Passwords: every seeded account that does not have its own quoted password uses 'Valid-password-123!'.\n\nAccounts: alice-dev / alice.dev@example.test, org-owner / org-owner@example.test, existing-member / existing-member@example.test, new-member / new-member@example.test, org-member / org-member@example.test, protected-member / protected-member@example.test, repo-admin / repo-admin@example.test, team-maintainer / team-maintainer@example.test, bob-reviewer / bob-reviewer@example.test, recovery-success / recovery-success@exam