{
 "architecture": "Architecture\n(1) Navigation map.\nFrontend is an SPA under frontend/src/App.tsx. The shell (components/AppShell.tsx) renders a top header with a Home logo link (name \"Home\"), a global repository search form (input aria-label \"Search\" and submit button \"Search\"), and the account menu in the upper-right. The account menu button displays the signed-in username when a session exists; its menu contains links/buttons \"Your organizations\", \"Settings\", and \"Sign out\". Visitors see \"Sign up\", \"Sign in\", and \"Forgot password\" as links on the home page. The home page (route \"/\") for visitors shows public repositories and public organizations as links named by the repository route (owner/name) or organization display name. After sign-in the same route shows \"Repositories\" (all repositories the current user can read, as owner/name links), \"Your organizations\" link, and a \"New repository\" button. Auth routes: /login (fields \"Username or email\" and \"Password\", button \"Sign in\"), /signup (fields \"Username\", \"Email\", \"Password\", button \"Create account\"), /password_reset (field \"Email\", button \"Send password reset email\"; after submit shows \"Verification code\", \"New password\", \"Confirm new password\", button \"Reset password\"). Account security: /settings (fields \"Current password\", \"New password\", \"Confirm new password\", button \"Update password\"). Organizations: /orgs (\"Your organizations\" page, \"New organization\" button), /orgs/new (fields \"Organization name\", \"Display name\", button \"Create organization\"), /orgs/:org (organization overview; heading is the organization display name; navigation links \"Repositories\", \"People\", \"Teams\"), /orgs/:org/repositories, /orgs/:org/people (member list with Member/Owner roles; \"Add member\" button and per-row \"Remove\" button), /orgs/:org/teams (team list; \"New team\" button), /orgs/:org/teams/new (field \"Team name\", button \"Create team\"), /orgs/:org/teams/:team (team detail, member management, parent/child team controls). Repositories: /new (\"New repository\" form: \"Owner\", \"Repository name\", \"Description\", \"Public\", \"Private\", \"Initialize this repository with a README\", button \"Create repository\"), /search?q= (repository search results as links), /:owner/:repo (repository overview and default Code tab; heading \"owner/name\"; shows owner, name, \"Public\"/\"Private\", description, default branch; repo navigation links \"Code\", \"Issues\", \"Pull requests\", \"Settings\"; also a clone URL with a \"Copy\" button). Code: /:owner/:repo/tree/:branch/* (file/directory browser; current branch selector is a button labelled with the branch name; \"Commits\" link; \"Add file\" button), /:owner/:repo/blob/:branch/* (file page, \"Edit\" button), /:owner/:repo/edit/:branch/* (file editing; fields \"Commit message\", \"Commit changes\"), /:owner/:repo/new/:branch/* (add file; fields \"File name\", \"Commit message\", \"Commit changes\"), /:owner/:repo/commits/:branch (commit history, reverse chronological), /:owner/:repo/commit/:sha (commit detail and diff), /:owner/:repo/compare/:base...:compare (comparison page), /:owner/:repo/search?q= (code search page; input \"Search code\", button \"Search\"), /:owner/:repo/branches (branch list, search input \"Find branch\", button \"New branch\"; new-branch form fields \"Branch name\", \"From\", button \"Create branch\"). Repository settings: /:owner/:repo/settings (general; visibility choices \"Public\"/\"Private\" and \"Save\"), /:owner/:repo/settings/access (\"Manage access\" page; grants for people and teams), /:owner/:repo/settings/branches (branch protection; button \"Add branch protection rule\", form fields \"Branch name pattern\", checkbox \"Require a pull request before merging\", \"Require approvals\", \"Require status checks\", button \"Create\"). Issues: /:owner/:repo/issues (list; rows show number, title, Open/Closed status, author, labels; filters \"Open\" and \"Closed\"; button \"New issue\"), /:owner/:repo/issues/new (fields \"Title\", \"Description\", button \"Submit new issue\"), /:owner/:repo/issues/:number (detail; title heading, status, right sidebar in order \"Assignees\", \"Labels\", \"Milestone\"; main description, comments, activity timeline; buttons \"Edit issue title\", \"Edit issue description\", \"Comment\", \"Close issue\"/\"Reopen issue\"; assignee controls and label/milestone selections use the quoted sidebar names). Pull requests: /:owner/:repo/pulls (list; rows show number, title, author, source/target branches, status; filters \"Open\" and \"Closed\"; button \"New pull request\"), /:owner/:repo/compare (comparison page with selects \"base\" and \"compare\" and button \"Compare changes\"; after comparison, fields \"Title\" and \"Description\", buttons \"Create pull request\" and \"Create draft pull request\"), /:owner/:repo/pull/:number (PR detail; title heading, visible status; navigation links \"Conversation\", \"Commits\", \"Files changed\", \"Checks\"; actions depend on status: \"Ready for review\", \"Merge pull request\" (with confirmation dialog button \"Confirm\"), \"Close pull request\"/\"Reopen pull request\", \"Approve\", \"Comment\", \"Add comment\", \"Add single comment\").\n\n(2) One data model.\nAll backend modules read/write one persisted JSON database via backend/src/store.js (loadJson/saveJson on dataDir/db.json). Collections: users {id, username, email, passwordHash, verified, createdAt}; sessions {id, userId, expiresAt}; organizations {id, name, displayName, createdAt}; memberships {id, organizationId, userId, role: \"Owner\"|\"Member\", createdAt}; teams {id, organizationId, name, parentTeamId|null, createdAt}; teamMemberships {id, teamId, userId}; repositories {id, ownerType: \"user\"|\"org\", ownerId, name, description, visibility, defaultBranch, forkedFromId|null, createdAt}; repositoryRoles {id, repositoryId, subjectType: \"user\"|\"team\", subjectId, role: \"Read\"|\"Triage\"|\"Write\"|\"Maintain\"|\"Admin\"}; branches {id, repositoryId, name, commitId, files: {path: {content, commitId}}}; commits {id, repositoryId, parentId|null, authorId, message, timestamp, changes: [{path, oldContent, newContent}]}; labels {id, repositoryId, name, color}; milestones {id, repositoryId, title}; issues {id, repositoryId, number, title, description, authorId, state, assigneeIds: [], labelIds: [], milestoneId|null, createdAt, updatedAt}; issueComments {id, issueId, authorId, body, createdAt}; issueEvents {id, issueId, type, userId, createdAt, metadata}; pullRequests {id, repositoryId, number, title, description, authorId, baseBranch, compareBranch, baseCommitId, currentCompareCommitId, status: \"draft\"|\"open\"|\"closed\"|\"merged\", createdAt, updatedAt}; prComments {id, pullRequestId, authorId, body, createdAt}; reviews {id, pullRequestId, reviewerId, decision, body, stale, createdAt}; reviewComments {id, pullRequestId, path, line, body, authorId, commitId, outdated, createdAt}; branchProtectionRules {id, repositoryId, pattern, requiredReviews, requiredStatusChecks}; repoSearch is derived from repositories and files, no separate store. A repo number is scoped per repository. A PR's current compare commit updates when its compare branch receives a new commit; merge eligibility is recalculated from branch protection rules and reviews.\n\n(3) Seed plan.\nEvery account uses password hash of \"Valid-password-123!\" unless noted; accounts without a quoted password also receive that password. Users: alice-dev (alice.dev@example.test), issue-editor (issue-editor@example.test), bob-reviewer (bob-reviewer@example.test), org-owner (org-owner@example.test), pr-contributor (pr-contributor@example.test), existing-member (existing-member@example.test), pr-author (pr-author@example.test), pr-reviewer (pr-reviewer@example.test), default-branch-admin (default-branch-admin@example.test), default-branch-viewer (default-branch-viewer@example.test), branch-contributor (branch-contributor@example.test), file-contributor (file-contributor@example.test), collaborator (collaborator@example.test), fork-user (fork-user@example.test), draft-author (draft-author@example.test). Organization acme-demo display name \"Acme Demo\" owned by org-owner (Owner); existing-member and bob-reviewer are Members. Teams in acme-demo: frontend-team, frontend-child (parent frontend-team), access-role-team; frontend-team contains existing-member; frontend-child contains bob-reviewer. Repositories: acme-docs (public, owner Acme Demo, default branch main, files README.md and src/search.ts, branches main, feature-search, branch-switch-demo, draft-feature), secret-research (private, owner Acme Demo, default branch main), default-branch-demo (public, owner default-branch-admin, default branch main, branches main and develop), file-management-demo (public, owner file-contributor, default branch main, README.md), branch-protection-demo (public, owner bob-reviewer, default branch main, branches main and test), acme-docs-fork (public, owner fork-user, forkedFrom acme-docs). Direct repository roles: issue-editor Admin on acme-docs; pr-contributor, pr-author, pr-reviewer, draft-author Write on acme-docs; bob-reviewer Admin on acme-docs and owner/Admin on branch-protection-demo; default-branch-admin Admin on default-branch-demo; default-branch-viewer Read on default-branch-demo; branch-contributor Write on default-branch-demo; file-contributor owner/Admin on file-management-demo; collaborator Admin on secret-research; fork-user owner/Admin on acme-docs-fork. Labels on acme-docs include bug, documentation, enhancement; milestone on acme-docs is v1.0. Issues in acme-docs: open issue \"Improve onboarding\" with description \"Describe the onboarding improvement.\", closed issue \"Fix login\", \"Editable onboarding issue\", \"Commentable onboarding issue\", \"Comment validation issue\", \"Assignable onboarding issue\", \"Closable onboarding issue\"; labels/milestones/assignees are left in an unset initial state on the mutation-scenario issues so tests can set them. Pull requests in acme-docs: open PR \"Improve onboarding\" (base main, compare feature-search), \"Reviewable onboarding PR\", \"Change request onboarding PR\", draft PR \"Draft onboarding update\" (author draft-author, base main, compare draft-feature), \"Closable onboarding PR\"; branch-protection-demo has PR \"Blocked onboarding PR\" (base test, compare fix-search) and PR \"Fix search\" (base test, compare fix-search, eligible). Branch protection rule on branch-protection-demo's test branch: pattern \"test\", requiredReviews 1, requiredStatusChecks 1. Quoted invalid names (-invalid-demo, -invalid-organization, -invalid-team, invalid..branch, ../invalid.md, invalid.email, unknown@example.test, 000000, does-not-match, Valid-password-123!-wrong) are not seeded as valid records; they are user inputs used by tests to exercise validation failures.\n\n(4) API endpoints grouped by backend module.\nauth.js: POST /api/auth/register {username,email,password}; POST /api/auth/login {usernameOrEmail,password}; POST /api/auth/logout; POST /api/auth/forgot-password {email}; POST /api/auth/reset-password {email,code,newPassword}; GET /api/auth/session; PATCH /api/auth/password {currentPassword,newPassword}. orgs.js: GET /api/orgs; POST /api/orgs {name,displayName}; GET /api/orgs/:org; GET /api/orgs/:org/repositories; GET /api/orgs/:org/members; POST /api/orgs/:org/members {username}; DELETE /api/orgs/:org/members/:username; GET /api/orgs/:org/teams; POST /api/orgs/:org/teams {name}; GET /api/orgs/:org/teams/:team; PATCH /api/orgs/:org/teams/:team {name,parentTeamId}; POST /api/orgs/:org/teams/:team/members {username}; DELETE /api/orgs/:org/teams/:team/members/:username. repos.js: GET /api/search/repositories?q=; GET /api/repositories (accessible list); POST /api/repositories {owner,name,description,visibility,initReadme}; GET /api/repositories/:owner/:repo; POST /api/repositorie
