{
 "architecture": "1. NAVIGATION MAP\nFrontend routes (react-router-dom 7):\n- '/' -> frontend/src/pages/HomePage.tsx (home / workbook list)\n- '/spreadsheets/d/:workbookId/edit' -> frontend/src/pages/EditorPage.tsx (workbook editor; Google Sheets shaped URL; optional '#gid=:sheetId' selects a worksheet)\n- No separate sign-in page. The requirements name no accounts, so there is no signed-in landing page; the home page is the public entry point and lists every workbook.\n\nHomePage:\n- h1 'Workbooks'.\n- Button 'New workbook' -> POST /api/workbooks, then navigate to the new editor URL.\n- Button 'Import CSV' (a file input labelled 'Import CSV') -> read the selected .csv text, POST /api/workbooks/import, then navigate to the new editor URL.\n- The main list shows every workbook as a link whose accessible name is exactly the workbook name (seed: 'Q3 Sales'). Under each name show 'Last updated <timestamp>'. Clicking the name opens '/spreadsheets/d/:id/edit'.\n- After create, rename, or import, returning to or refreshing '/' reloads this list from GET /api/workbooks.\n\nEditorPage:\n- Top bar: link 'Back to workbooks' -> '/'; h1 is the workbook name; button 'Rename workbook' opens an in-page dialog (role=dialog) with input labelled 'Workbook name' and buttons 'Save' and 'Cancel'.\n- Toolbar buttons: 'Undo', 'Redo', 'Export CSV', 'Data'.\n- 'Data' opens a menu whose commands use role=menuitem: 'Sort range...', 'Filter', 'Data validation', 'Pivot table'. All dialogs opened from this menu use role=dialog and option elements with role=option in named combo boxes.\n- Formula bar: a text input with accessible name 'Formula bar'. It shows the formula of the active cell when the active cell has a formula, otherwise its literal value.\n- Worksheet grid: the active worksheet is a region with role=grid, aria-label='Worksheet grid', aria-multiselectable='true'. Column headers use role=columnheader with accessible names A, B, C, ... . Row headers use role=rowheader with accessible names 1, 2, 3, ... . Cells use role=gridcell with accessible names A1, B2, etc. The active cell and every cell in the currently selected rectangular range expose aria-selected='true'; all other cells expose aria-selected='false'.\n- Double-clicking a grid cell shows an inline text input with accessible name 'Edit <coordinate>', e.g. 'Edit A1'. Editing through the grid, through 'Formula bar', or through paste commits through PUT/PATCH cell/range APIs.\n- Sheet tab bar at the bottom: each worksheet is a role=tab button whose accessible name is the worksheet name; the active tab has aria-selected='true'. Each tab also has a button with accessible name 'Worksheet options for <worksheet name>', which opens a menu with role=menuitem commands 'Rename' and 'Delete'. A button with accessible name 'Add worksheet' creates the next worksheet and switches to it. Sheet order equals the order of the tab list, persisted in the workbook.\n- Right-clicking a row header opens a menu with menuitems 'Insert row above', 'Insert row below', 'Delete row'. Right-clicking a column header opens 'Insert column left', 'Insert column right', 'Delete column'. Right-clicking a cell opens a cell context menu with 'Cut', 'Copy', 'Paste'.\n- After any mutation, the frontend replaces its workbook state from the response. A direct reload of '/spreadsheets/d/:id/edit' fetches GET /api/workbooks/:id and renders the same workbook, the same worksheet order, and the persisted active worksheet.\n\n2. DATA MODEL (one shared persisted store, implemented by backend/src/store.js; loaded/saved with loadJson/saveJson)\nCollections: the single JSON store contains one top-level array 'workbooks'. There are no users, accounts, memberships, or permissions.\n\nWorkbook:\n{\n  id: string,\n  name: string,\n  createdAt: string,\n  updatedAt: string,\n  activeSheetId: string,\n  history: { undo: Operation[], redo: Operation[] },\n  sheets: Sheet[],\n  pivotTables: PivotTable[]\n}\n\nSheet:\n{\n  id: string,\n  name: string,\n  rowCount: number,\n  colCount: number,\n  cells: Record<Coord, Cell>,\n  validations: Validation[],\n  sort: SortState | null,\n  filter: FilterState | null\n}\n\nCell:\n{ v?: string|number|boolean, f?: string }\n- 'v' stores the literal value, or the computed result for a formula cell.\n- 'f' stores the original formula text (e.g. '=A1+B1') exactly as submitted.\n- Empty cells are absent from 'cells'.\n\nCoord: A1-style, 1-based (e.g. 'A1', 'B2').\nValidation: { id, range, type: 'dropdown'|'number', options?: string[], min?: number, max?: number }\nSortState: { range, column, order: 'asc'|'desc' }\nFilterState: { range, column, criteria: { values?: Array<string|number>, condition?: string, value?: string|number } }\nPivotTable: { id, name, sourceSheetId, sourceRange, rowField, valueField, aggregation: 'sum'|'count'|'average', resultSheetId }\n\nRelationships and invariants:\n- sheets belong to one workbook by containment; activeSheetId must reference an existing sheet in the same workbook.\n- pivotTables belong to a workbook; sourceSheetId and resultSheetId reference sheets in the same workbook.\n- Row/column insertion and deletion shift all cell coordinates, formula references (relative references adjust; absolute references do not), validation ranges, sort ranges, filter ranges, and pivot source ranges by the same translation rules.\n- The default blank grid is 30 rows x 26 columns.\n- Formula evaluation happens centrally: cells.js, sheets.js, and analyze.js all call formulas.js after any change that affects source values or structure. One erroneous formula produces an error string in its own 'v' (e.g. '#DIV/0!', '#VALUE!', '#REF!') and does not alter unrelated cells.\n- Undo/redo operations are serialized into workbook.history and persist after refresh. Every mutating endpoint pushes an undo operation before applying the mutation and clears redo; undo/redo apply inverse operations and recalculate.\n\n3. SEED PLAN (created by backend/src/seed.js only when the store file does not exist)\nSeed exactly one workbook:\n- Workbook id 'wb-q3-sales', name 'Q3 Sales', activeSheetId 'sheet-1'.\n- Sheet id 'sheet-1', name 'Sheet1', rowCount 30, colCount 26.\n- Cells: A1='Region', B1='Sales', C1='Status', A2='East', B2=1200, C2='Open', A3='North', B3=800, C3='Closed', A4='South', B4=700, C4='Open'.\n- No Sheet2 is seeded; tests create it through 'Add worksheet' where the requirement expects a second worksheet.\n- No users/passwords/memberships are seeded.\n- Values quoted only as user/test entry (A1:B2, D1:E2, Item/Qty, Pen/4, A1=2, B1=3, =A1+B1, =C1*2, A1:C6 as a selected range, etc.) are not seed content; they are entered through the UI by the scenarios that need them.\n\n4. API ENDPOINTS (all handled in backend/src/app.js; grouped by backend module)\nAll JSON errors are { error: string } with 400/404/409. Every mutating JSON endpoint returns the complete updated workbook document in { workbook }, except export.\n\nWorkbooks module (backend/src/workbooks.js):\n- GET /api/workbooks -> 200 { workbooks: [{ id, name, updatedAt, sheetCount, activeSheetId }] }\n- POST /api/workbooks, body { name? } -> 201 { workbook }; creates one blank workbook with one 'Sheet1'; default name 'Untitled spreadsheet'.\n- POST /api/workbooks/import, body { name?, csv } -> 201 { workbook }; parses CSV into Sheet1, sets rowCount/colCount from the CSV extent, default name from 'name' else 'Imported workbook'. This literal route is matched before /api/workbooks/:id.\n- GET /api/workbooks/:id -> 200 { workbook }\n- PATCH /api/workbooks/:id, body { name } -> 200 { workbook }; renames workbook.\n- GET /api/workbooks/:id/export.csv?sheetId=... -> 200 text/csv; if sheetId is absent uses activeSheetId; exports only that worksheet; does not mutate workbook state.\n\nSheets module (backend/src/sheets.js):\n- POST /api/workbooks/:id/sheets, body { name? } -> 201 { workbook }; default name 'SheetN', new sheet becomes active.\n- PATCH /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId, body { name } -> 200 { workbook }\n- DELETE /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId -> 200 { workbook }; 409 if it is the last worksheet.\n- POST /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/rows, body { at, count? } -> 200 { workbook }; inserts count rows before 1-based row number 'at'.\n- DELETE /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/rows, body { at, count? } -> 200 { workbook }\n- POST /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/columns, body { at, count? } -> 200 { workbook }; inserts before 1-based column number 'at' (1 = column A).\n- DELETE /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/columns, body { at, count? } -> 200 { workbook }\n\nCells module (backend/src/cells.js):\n- PUT /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/cells/:cellId, body { value } -> 200 { workbook }; if value starts with '=', store f; otherwise store v; recalculate and validate.\n- PATCH /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/range, body { start, values: CellValue[][] } -> 200 { workbook }; writes a rectangular range starting at 'start'.\n- POST /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/range/transfer, body { source, target, cut } -> 200 { workbook }; copies or moves a rectangular range, adjusts relative references, clears source when cut, moves exact validation rules when cut, and recalculates.\n\nHistory module (backend/src/history.js):\n- POST /api/workbooks/:id/undo -> 200 { workbook }\n- POST /api/workbooks/:id/redo -> 200 { workbook }\n\nData/analysis module (backend/src/analyze.js):\n- POST /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/sort, body { range, column, order: 'asc'|'desc' } -> 200 { workbook }; physically reorders rows only within the selected range.\n- PUT /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/filter, body { range, column, criteria: { values?: Array<string|number>, condition?: string, value?: string|number } } -> 200 { workbook }; stores the filter and changes only row visibility.\n- DELETE /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/filter -> 200 { workbook }\n- PUT /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/validations, body { id?, range, type: 'dropdown'|'number', options?, min?, max? } -> 200 { workbook }; creates/updates a validation rule.\n- DELETE /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/validations/:validationId -> 200 { workbook }\n- POST /api/workbooks/:id/sheets/:sheetId/pivot-tables, body { sourceRange, rowField, valueField, aggregation } -> 201 { workbook }; creates a new result worksheet and writes the current pivot grid.\n- POST /api/workbooks/:id/pivot-tables/:pivotId/refresh -> 200 { workbook }; recomputes the result worksheet from the current source range without modifying source values or order.\n\n5. SESSIONS/PERMISSIONS\nNo sessions, auth cookies, roles, or memberships are implemented because the requirements name no accounts or passwords. All APIs are public and every route works anonymously; the home page lists all workbooks. If a host environment imposes a sign-in wall, no requirement-scenario credential exists to use it, so the hosted shell should treat the app as fully accessible.\n\n6. REQUIREMENT OWNERSHIP BY MODULE\n- workbooks.js: REQ-1, REQ-1-1-1, REQ-1-2-1, REQ-1-2-2, REQ-1-3-1, REQ-1-3-2.\n- sheets.js: REQ-2, REQ-2-1-1, REQ-2-1-2, REQ-2-1-3, REQ-2-1-4, REQ-2-2-1, REQ-2-2-2.\n- cells.js: REQ-3, REQ-3-1-1, REQ-3-1-2, REQ-3-1-3, REQ-3-2-1.\n- history.js: REQ-3-2-2; it also provides undo/redo coverage for row/column, formula, validation, and pivot result changes.\n- formulas.js: REQ-4, REQ-4-1-1, REQ-4-1-2, REQ-4-2-1, REQ-4-2-2.\n- analyze.js: REQ-5, REQ-5-1-1, REQ-5-1-2, REQ-5-2-1, REQ-5-3-1.\n- store.js and seed.js are shared by all modules; app.js only wires routes to modules. Frontend files stay small: App.tsx, pages/HomePage.tsx, pages/EditorPage.tsx, components/WorkbookGrid.tsx, FormulaBar.tsx, SheetTabs.tsx, Toolbar.tsx, menus/ContextMenu.tsx, and per-feature dialogs under components/dialogs/.",
